From 0e1552d7cb42007577dde03d02ae37bf51750f23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:51:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 2 fix: enforce sequential single-position trades in
 exit-policy backtest

Martin flagged that the exit-policy backtest counted an entry episode as a
new trade even while a previously simulated trade (for the same symbol/
candidate) was still open -- entries are detected purely from the regime
condition re-firing, with no gating on whether a prior trade had actually
closed. Since trades can hold up to --max-hold-hours (default 240h), this
meant the backtest could effectively simulate multiple concurrent positions
in the same instrument, which no real single-position account could ever
hold. It also explained why trade_summary's cumulative max-drawdown numbers
looked implausibly large: they summed per-trade returns in entry order as
if each trade sequentially added to one account curve, which isn't valid
when trades overlap in time.

Fix: simulate_trades_for_entries now walks entries in chronological order
and skips (drops, does not defer) any entry that fires before the
previously-taken trade's own exit_ts, evaluated independently per policy in
the grid since a wider trailing stop holds a position open longer than a
tighter one. simulate_trade now returns the trade's exit_ts (the bar where
STOP/TARGET fired, or the last bar for TIMEOUT/NO_DATA_AFTER_ENTRY) to make
this possible. Every result row, walk-forward fold, and the report.txt
per-row summary line now report entries_skipped_overlap / entries_total so
the skip rate is always visible rather than silently lowering trade counts.

4 new tests cover the gating directly (skip while open, take after close,
resume correctly after a skip, and that skip count is computed per-policy
since hold duration differs by policy). All 25 previously-existing tests
in this file still pass unmodified -- this only changes trade counts when
entries actually overlap in time, not the per-trade simulation logic.

Research only, no live/paper execution touched -- same invariants as the
original Phase 2 patch (.19/.22/.23 live execution path untouched,
VALIDATED_LONG_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS / VALIDATED_SHORT_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS
remain frozenset()).

